# 17. API DESIGN RULES

Every API should define:

- HTTP method
- Endpoint
- Authentication
- Permission
- Request DTO
- Validation
- Response DTO
- Error codes
- Business rules
- Audit behavior
- Transaction behavior

Example:

POST /api/patients

Request:

{
  "firstName": "...",
  "lastName": "...",
  "dateOfBirth": "...",
  "phone": "..."
}

Response:

{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": "...",
    "mrn": "..."
  }
}

---

# 18. API STATUS CODES

200
Successful request

201
Created

204
Successful request without response body

400
Validation error

401
Unauthenticated

403
Unauthorized

404
Resource not found

409
Business conflict

422
Semantic validation

429
Rate limited

500
Unexpected server error

---

