# 60. GIT WORKFLOW

main
    production

develop
    integration

feature/*
    new feature

fix/*
    bug fix

release/*
    release preparation

Typical workflow:

Create branch
 ↓
Develop
 ↓
Test
 ↓
Commit
 ↓
Pull Request
 ↓
Code Review
 ↓
CI
 ↓
Merge

---

# 61. COMMIT STYLE

Recommended:

feat: add patient registration
feat: add appointment scheduling
fix: correct payment validation
fix: prevent duplicate patient creation
refactor: simplify appointment service
test: add patient registration e2e
docs: update API documentation
chore: update dependencies

---

# 62. DOCUMENTATION UPDATE RULE

Whenever behavior changes:

1. Update SRS if requirement changes.
2. Update flow.
3. Update Figma.
4. Update database documentation.
5. Update API documentation.
6. Update implementation.
7. Update tests.
8. Update changelog.

Documentation must remain synchronized with software.

---

# 63. DEFINITION OF DONE

A feature is DONE only when:

[ ] Requirement understood
[ ] Flow documented
[ ] Figma designed
[ ] Database implemented
[ ] API implemented
[ ] Backend implemented
[ ] Frontend implemented
[ ] Validation implemented
[ ] Authorization implemented
[ ] Error states implemented
[ ] Audit implemented where required
[ ] Real-time implemented where required
[ ] Unit tests pass
[ ] Integration tests pass
[ ] E2E tests pass where applicable
[ ] Responsive behavior verified
[ ] Documentation updated
[ ] Code reviewed
[ ] Staging verified
[ ] UAT accepted

